@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Me";
}

<div class="hero" style="min-height: auto; padding: 4rem 1rem 3rem;">
    <div class="hero-content" style="max-width: 1000px; width: 100%;">
        <h1 class="hero-title">Hey, I'm Trae.</h1>

        <div class="verse-box text-start" style="max-width: 100%;">
            <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #ddd;">
                I help people with their computers and Wi-Fi. I'm finishing my school degrees in
                computer safety (called cybersecurity), and I started England Technologies LLC.
                I live near Jacksonville, Florida.
            </p>
            <p style="color: #aaa; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                Tech can feel confusing, and a lot of people get talked down to about it. I don't do that.
                My promise is to explain things in plain words, so you know what was wrong, what I did,
                and why. I work best when I get to know you first, so I can explain things in a way that
                makes sense to you. Ask me as many questions as you like.
            </p>
            <div class="d-flex gap-2 justify-content-center flex-wrap">
                <a class="btn btn-outline-info" style="color: var(--et-accent, #00bfff) !important;" href="/contact">Book Online</a>
                <a class="btn btn-outline-light" style="color: var(--et-btn-text, #e0e0e0) !important;" href="tel:+19042580217">Call 904-258-0217</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="container py-4">
    <h2 class="mb-2" style="color: #00bfff;">What I Do</h2>
    <p class="mb-3" style="color: #aaa;">
        I fix slow computers, remove viruses, set up new devices, get Wi-Fi working in every room,
        and help you save your photos and files. For fun, I also build my own set-up at home, with the
        same kind of equipment a business uses. That way I can test a fix before I bring it to you.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-3" style="color: #aaa;">
        I use Linux every day. I'm also comfortable with Windows and Mac computers.
        I like to keep things private and in my own hands, which is why I run many of my own tools
        instead of handing your information to big companies.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="container py-4">
    <h2 class="mb-2" style="color: #00bfff;">Lab Environment</h2>
    <p class="mb-3" style="color: #aaa;">
        My home set-up is a fast desktop computer and a few extra computers that store files and run
        the internet connection. They sit behind a strong digital wall, called a firewall, that keeps
        bad guys out. This is where I practice and test things.
        </p>
    <a class="btn btn-outline-info" style="color: var(--et-accent, #00bfff) !important;" href="https://englandtechnologies.net/Docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        See the technical details (for the curious)
    </a>
</section>

<section class="container py-4 pb-5">
    <h2 class="mb-3" style="color: #00bfff;">Education</h2>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li><strong>Master's degree in Cybersecurity</strong> (computer safety), University of Florida. I'm working on this now.</li>
            <li><strong>Bachelor's degree in Information Technology</strong> (computer safety and running computer systems), University of North Florida. Finished December 2025.</li>
        </ul>
    </div></div>
</section>
